DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context()->variables->add(A => "Real");

$ans1 = Formula("sin(A)/cos(A)");
$ans2 = Formula("2*cos^2(A)");
$ans3 = Formula("1");
$ans4 = Formula("sin^2(A)");
$ans5 = Formula("2*sin^2(A)");
$ans6 = Formula("sin(A)");
$ans7 = Formula("2*sin^3(A)");

BEGIN_PGML

Fill in the blanks below appropriately to obtain a proof for the expression


[``` \tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A)) = \sin(A) - 2\sin^3(A) ```]

*Proof:*

[`` \tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A)) = ``] [_]{$ans1} [`` \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A)) ``]

[`` \phantom{\tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A))} = \sin(A) \cdot ( ``] [_]{$ans2}  [`` - ``] [_]{$ans3} [`` ) ``]

[`` \phantom{\tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A))} = \sin(A) \cdot ( 2  - 2\cdot``] [_]{$ans4}  [`` - 1 ) ``]

[`` \phantom{\tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A))} = \sin(A) \cdot ( 1  - ``] [_]{$ans5}  [`` ) ``]

[`` \phantom{\tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A))} = ``] [_]{$ans6}  [`` - ``] [_]{$ans7}

[`` \phantom{\tan(A) \cdot (2\cos^3(A)-\cos(A))} = \sin(A) - 2\sin^3(A) ``]

_Your goal is to fill in the blanks with appropriate formulas to make adjacent expressions equal._

_There may be other ways to prove the original identity but this problem requires the correct logic using this approach._

END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();
